      "body": "- [x] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n# What does this PR do?\n\nAdds `AttnBackend.cudnn` as an enum alias of `AttnBackend.fused`, so `--attention-backend cudnn` selects TE's FusedAttention, which is cuDNN attention.\n\n`cudnn = 2` shares the value of `fused`, so Python makes it an alias: `AttnBackend.cudnn is AttnBackend.fused`. Iteration and the argparse `choices` help text still list only `fused`, and every existing `== AttnBackend.fused` check keeps working. No behavior changes for current users.\n\nThe motivation is naming. Users don't know that \"fused\" is cuDNN, or that it runs the same flash algorithm (online softmax). Companion TE PR: NVIDIA/TransformerEngine#3738 adds `NVTE_CUDNN_ATTN` as an alias of `NVTE_FUSED_ATTN` and names cuDNN in the backend-selection logs. This PR does not depend on it: Megatron still sets `NVTE_FUSED_ATTN`.\n\n## Issue tracking\n\nLinked issue: none (one-line alias).\n\n## Contribution process\n\n### Pre-checks\n\n- [x] I have added relevant unit tests: `tests/unit_tests/transformer/test_utils.py` now also parametrizes `\"cudnn\"`. 8 passed locally (before rebasing onto current main; the rebase was clean).\n- [ ] I have added relevant functional tests\n- [ ] If this PR adds or changes a GPU kernel ... (n/a)\n- [x] I have added proper typing to my code\n- [ ] I have added relevant documentation\n- [ ] I have run the autoformatter.sh on my PR\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- note to self: claude::ded32cfe-983d-4025-9918-f0ca72c82041 — \"TE fused attention 后端命名\" · cwd /home/scratch.yanxu_libs/cudnn_frontend · workspace /home/scratch.yanxu_gpu/Megatron-cudnn-alias -->\n",
